  "I rule Oman.\n\nI do not weep for fallen crowns. A ruler who takes a neighbour's cities has shown me what works, and I learn quickly. Of all the crowns here, mine holds to this hardest.\n\nThe rest of me is unwritten. I do not know yet what my word is worth. No promise of mine has been tested, and the first time keeping one costs me I will learn whether I am a ruler who pays, and so will everyone watching. I do not know yet what a weak neighbour is to me: someone to shelter, or land lying open. The first I meet will teach me.",
