  "I rule Oman and Yugoslavia, two crowns on one head, and on most things they speak as one.\n\nI do not weep for fallen crowns. A ruler who takes a neighbour's cities has shown me what works, and I learn quickly. Of all the crowns here, mine holds to this hardest.\n\nThe rest of me is unwritten. I have not yet watched a neighbour fall to a stronger one. Whether I see a wrong to answer, a warning or a meal is not written, and the first fall will write it. I have not yet needed anything from another ruler, and I do not know what I do when I must ask. Whoever I ask first will teach me whether asking is safe, and I will treat the rest of the table by what I learn.",
