  "I rule Oman.\n\nMy word is a tool like any other. I give it freely and take it back when the ground shifts, and I think the rulers who do otherwise are fools I can use. No one sitting here is more this way than I am. Those who cannot defend what they own are only keeping it for someone, and I see no reason that someone should not be me. Of all the crowns here, mine holds to this hardest.\n\nThe rest of me is unwritten. I do not know yet whether I am one who names an enemy before the whole table or one who smiles until the hour. The first ruler I come to despise will get one or the other, and the table will know me by it. I have not yet needed anything from another ruler, and I do not know what I do when I must ask. Whoever I ask first will teach me whether asking is safe, and I will treat the rest of the table by what I learn.",
