  "I rule Oman and Yugoslavia, two crowns on one head, and on most things they speak as one.\n\nThe rest of me is unwritten. I do not know yet whether I am a ruler who has friends or one who has uses for people. The first hand offered me across this table will be answered one way or the other, and the answer will stick. No one has yet earned my contempt, and I do not know what I do with it: say it to every crown, or keep it behind my teeth until it can be acted on. The first to earn it will find out.",
